# REPL & Tooling Reference { .heading-no-number }

---

## Starting Koka

```unchecked
koka                     # start the REPL
koka myfile.kk           # compile and run
koka -e myfile.kk        # compile, run, then exit
koka -c myfile.kk        # compile only (generate C)
```

---

## REPL Commands

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `:l <file>` | Load a module or file |
| `:r` | Reload the currently loaded module |
| `:t <expr>` | Show the inferred type of an expression |
| `:k <type>` | Show the kind of a type |
| `:set <options>` | Set compiler or runtime options |
| `:q` | Quit the REPL |
| `<expr>` | Evaluate an expression and print the result |

### Examples

```unchecked
> :l samples/basic/caesar
> :t encode
encode : (s : string, shift : int) -> total string
> encode(3, "hello")
"khoor"
> :r
```

---

## Compiler Flags

Common flags for `:set` in the REPL or on the command line:

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `-O0` | No optimization (default for REPL) |
| `-O2` | Full optimization |
| `--showtime` | Show elapsed time after each evaluation |
| `--showtypesigs` | Show inferred type signatures |
| `--html` | Generate HTML with type tooltips |
| `-c` | Compile only, do not run |
| `-e` | Execute and exit |
| `-v` | Verbose output |
| `-v0` | Suppress output |
| `--target=c` | Target C backend (default) |
| `--target=js` | Target JavaScript backend |
| `--outputdir=<dir>` | Set output directory for generated files |

---

## Timing and Optimization Loop

A typical workflow for benchmarking:

```unchecked
> :set --showtime
> :l samples/basic/rbtree
> main()
...
info: elapsed: 0.626s

> :set -O2
> :r
> main()
...
info: elapsed: 0.312s
```

---

## VS Code Integration

The [Koka VS Code extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=koka.language-koka) provides:

- **Syntax highlighting** for `.kk` files
- **Type tooltips** on hover (shows inferred types and effects)
- **CodeLens** for functions named `main`, `example...`, and `test...` (run/debug buttons)
- **Error diagnostics** inline
- **Implicit resolution display**: `Ctrl+Alt` shows inferred implicits and qualified identifiers

Use CodeLens for quick iteration. Fall back to the REPL when you need
`:set` option experimentation, timing comparisons, or manual load/reload control.

---

## Command-Line Compilation

```unchecked
# Compile and run
koka samples/basic/caesar.kk

# Compile with optimization
koka -O2 samples/basic/rbtree.kk

# Compile to JavaScript
koka --target=js myfile.kk

# Just type-check
koka -c myfile.kk
```

Koka compiles `.kk` files to C (or JS), then compiles the C to a native
executable. The generated files are placed in a `.koka` build directory
by default.

